course: dictionary
lesson: 8232
title: Revive: bringing things back
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: To revive means to bring something back to life, strength or energy. It can be about a person who has fainted, or about a thing that was weak, forgotten or no longer used. The word starts with re-, which means again, so revive means to come back again.
explain: Use the words around it to find the meaning. «Flowers revive in water» tells you that a droopy flower can perk up again once it has a drink. In «revived interest», people who had stopped caring start to be keen once more. Ask yourself: what came back?
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Hebrew was revived as an everyday language around 1900» means that Hebrew was brought back to life as a language people used every day, so the meaning fits.
fact: Revive means to bring back to life, strength, popularity or energy.
fact: «Revive a tradition» means to bring an old custom back into use.
fact: About 7,000 languages are spoken today, and around 4 in 10 are endangered, so some need help to be revived.
fact: «Many Indigenous peoples are reviving their languages, rights and land.» Reviving means bringing something back to life or strength.
fact: Re- at the start of a word often means again, so it is a clue to the meaning of revive.
exercise: «The nurse used CPR to revive the man who had fainted.» What does revive mean here? | To put someone to sleep | *To bring someone back to consciousness | To paint someone's picture
exercise: «The old dance was revived at the school fair.» What does revived mean? | Cancelled for ever | Forgotten and hidden away | *Brought back into use and popularity
exercise: «Flowers revive in water.» What is happening to the flowers? | *They are getting fresh and full of energy again | They are being picked | They are turning into water | They are changing colour to black
test: «Some rotifers were reported to revive after about 24,000 years frozen in Siberian ice.» What does revive mean in this sentence? | Grow very large | Melt into water | Stay frozen for ever | *Come back to life
test: Which word has the same clue as revive, the prefix re- meaning again? | Unwrap | Forward | Enjoy | *Rewrite
exam: «Indigenous peoples are reviving their languages, rights and land.» Which meaning fits best? | Hiding things from others | Losing something bit by bit | *Bringing something back to strength and use | Moving to a new country
